{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And the parched ground.</b> A place of parched heat, and likewise לא יכס שרב ושמש (Isaiah 49:10), and likewise the Targum of אכלני (Genesis 31:40) [means] 'parched heat' in Aramaic." "<b>In the habitation.</b> Which was the habitation of jackals, and it is a place of dryness." "<b>Reed-grass.</b> Like 'court' [חצר]." "<b>For reed and rush.</b> That they will grow around the rivers."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 35, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:56:47.378924861Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}